 {
  "coord": "15:39",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "reversal",
  "note": "Seduced belongs to his wanton eye (Edward), not to the widow.",
  "replacement": "BUCKINGHAM. My lord, this shows conscience in your Grace. But the scruples behind it are petty and trivial, once everything is considered. You say that Edward is your brother's son. So do we, but not by Edward's wife. He was first contracted to Lady Lucy, and your mother is alive to witness his vow. Afterward he was betrothed by proxy to Bona, sister of the King of France. He broke off both. Then a poor petitioner, a mother of many sons worn out with cares, a widow whose beauty was fading and who was in distress, in the afternoon of her best days, became the prize and purchase of his lustful eye. That eye seduced the height and pitch of his rank down to a base decline and a loathsome bigamy. By her, in his unlawful bed, he fathered this Edward, whom we politely call the Prince. I could complain more bitterly, but out of respect for some who are still alive, I put a limit on my tongue. So, my good lord, take this offered dignity for yourself. If not to bless us and the land, then at least to draw your noble ancestry out of the corruption of abusing times and back onto a true line of descent."
 },
